/*!
\page page_sthelixmodel StHelixModel

\brief Concrete helix-based track geometry for a charged particle in STAR's solenoidal field.

\section sthelixmodel_overview Overview

\ref StHelixModel is the concrete implementation of \ref StTrackGeometry.  It stores
the five helix parameters (charge \e q, curvature \e κ, azimuthal angle \e ψ, dip angle
\e λ, and reference-point origin \b r₀), together with the full momentum vector
\b p and the helicity sign \e h.

\section sthelixmodel_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
StObject
  └── StTrackGeometry   (abstract)
           └── StHelixModel
\endcode

\section sthelixmodel_params Helix Parameterisation

| Symbol | Units | Physical Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| \e q | — | Electric charge (+1 or −1). |
| κ | cm⁻¹ | Signed curvature; \|κ\| = \|qB\|/p_T. |
| ψ | rad | Azimuthal angle of the momentum vector at the origin. |
| λ | rad | Dip angle: arctan(p_z/p_T). |
| **r**₀ | cm | Reference point (3-D PCA to primary vertex). |
| **p** | GeV/c | Momentum vector at **r**₀. |
| h | — | Helix sense: +1 = clockwise viewed along +z = −sign(qB_z). |

The phase passed to \c StPhysicalHelixD is φ₀ = ψ − h·π/2.

\section sthelixmodel_members Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \c mCharge | \c Short_t | Electric charge. |
| \c mCurvature | \c Float_t | Signed κ (cm⁻¹). |
| \c mPsi | \c Float_t | Azimuthal momentum angle ψ (rad). |
| \c mDipAngle | \c Float_t | Dip angle λ (rad). |
| \c mOrigin | \c StThreeVectorF | Reference point (cm). |
| \c mMomentum | \c StThreeVectorF | Momentum vector (GeV/c). |
| \c mHelicity | \c Short_t | Helix sense ±1. |

\section sthelixmodel_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StHelixModel* hm =
    dynamic_cast<const StHelixModel*>(track->geometry());
if (!hm) return;

double pt    = hm->momentum().perp();  // GeV/c
double kappa = hm->curvature();        // cm⁻¹
int    h     = hm->helicity();         // +1 or -1

StPhysicalHelixD helix = hm->helix();
double sAtR = helix.pathLength(100.0 /* cm */);
StThreeVectorD pos = helix.at(sAtR);
\endcode

\see StTrackGeometry
\see StTrack
*/
